Q: How to use custom fonts at Chakra v3 A: <p>This official guide for React (Vite) is the best info I found:
<a href="https://chakra-ui.com/guides/theming-add-custom-font-to-vite" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://chakra-ui.com/guides/theming-add-custom-font-to-vite</a></p>
<ol>
<li><p>Install the font from <a href="https://fontsource.org/" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://fontsource.org/</a>
(e.g. &quot;Bricolage Grotesque&quot;)</p>
</li>
<li><p>Import the font CSS: (main.tsx)</p>
</li>
</ol>
<p><code>import &quot;@fontsource-variable/bricolage-grotesque/index.css&quot;</code></p>
<ol start="3">
<li>Finally, pass the system into the ChakraProvider:
(components/ui/provider.tsx)</li>
</ol>
<pre><code>export function Provider(props: ColorModeProviderProps) {
  return (
    &lt;ChakraProvider value={system}&gt;
      &lt;ColorModeProvider {...props} /&gt;
    &lt;/ChakraProvider&gt;
  )
}
</code></pre>

Q: New app collides with status bar and the navigation bar of phone A: <p>You can change the settings in <code>capacitor.config.json</code> and set <code>android</code> → <code>adjustMarginsForEdgeToEdge</code> to <code>auto</code> or <code>force</code></p>
<p>No plugin is needed</p>
<p>It might look something like this:</p>
<pre><code>{
  &quot;appId&quot;: &quot;com.example.app&quot;,
  &quot;appName&quot;: &quot;ExampleName&quot;,
  &quot;webDir&quot;: &quot;www&quot;,
  &quot;android&quot;: {
    &quot;adjustMarginsForEdgeToEdge&quot;: &quot;auto&quot;
  }
}
</code></pre>
<hr />
<p>More info <a href="https://capacitorjs.com/docs/v7/config" rel="nofollow noreferrer">here</a> (search for adjustMarginsForEdgeToEdge)</p>
<p>In Capacitor 7 the default is <code>false</code>, but this has been changed to <code>auto</code> in version 8, and the setting has been removed</p>
<p><strong>Update:</strong> To get this to work in Capacitor 8 I had to add the following to <code>styles.css</code>:</p>
<pre><code>body{
    padding-top: env(safe-area-inset-top);
}
</code></pre>
<p>I hope this helps!</p>
